claim.claim-text:
CLAIMS A tunable laser, comprising: a base; a gain medium coupled to the base; a tunable feedback device coupled to said base to provide feedback of a selected wavelength to the gain medium; and a first compensating element providing the coupling to said base for at lease one of said gain medium and said tunable feedback device such that thermal expansion of the compensating element maintains a substantially constant integer number of half- wavelengths within a resonant cavity defined by the gain medium and the tunable feedback device during temperature variations in the tunable laser. 2. The tunable laser of Claim 1, wherein the tunable feedback device comprises: a diffraction element; and a tuning element coupled to said diffraction element to adjust an orientation of said diffraction element with respect to said gain medium to vary the selected wavelength. 3. The tunable laser of Claim 1, wherein the tunable feedback device comprises: a diffraction element having dispersion planes; a retroreflector within the dispersion planes; and a tuning element for adjusting an orientation of at least one of said diffraction element and said retroreflector to vary the selected wavelength. 4. The tunable laser of Claim 1, wherein the tunable feedback device comprises: an interference element; a retroreflector; and 

 a tuning element for adjusting an orientation of said interference element to vary the selected wavelength. 5. A tunable laser, comprising: a base; a gain medium coupled to the base; a tunable feedback device coupled to said base to provide feedback of a selected wavelength to the gain medium; a drive system coupled to said base and to said tunable feedback device for tuning said tunable feedback device to the selected wavelength; and a first compensating element integrated into said drive system such that thermal expansion of the compensating element offsets a difference in the expansion of the base and the drive system to maintain a substantially constant wavelength within a resonant cavity defined by the gain medium and the feedback device during temperature variations in the tunable laser. 6. The tunable laser of Claim 5, wherein the tunable feedback device comprises: a diffraction element coupled to said drive system such that a movement of said drive system varies an orientation of said diffraction element with respect to said gain medium to vary the selected wavelength. 7. The tunable laser of Claim 5, wherein the tunable feedback device comprises: a diffraction element having dispersion planes; a retroreflector within the dispersion planes; and at least one of said diffraction element and said retroreflector coupled to said drive system such that a movement of said drive system varies an orientation of at least one of said diffraction element and said retroreflector to vary the selected wavelength. 8. The tunable laser of Claim 5, wherein the tunable feedback device comprises: an interference element; 

 a retroreflector; and at least one of said interference element and said retroreflector coupled to said drive system such that a movement of said drive system varies an orientation of at least one of said diffraction element and said retroreflector to vary the selected wavelength. 9. A tunable laser, comprising: a base having an upper and lower surface and an aperture extending therethrough; a gain medium coupled to the upper surface of said base; a first feedback device coupled to the upper surface of said base to provide feedback of a selected wavelength to said gain medium; a pivot arm with a proximal and a distal end, and the proximal end of said pivot arm pivotally attached to the lower surface of said base at a first pivot axis normal to the upper surface of the base, and the distal end of said pivot arm extending through the aperture; such that an arcuate displacement of said pivot arm lies in a first plane substantially parallel to the upper surface; a second feedback device coupled to the distal end of said pivot arm to provide feedback of the selected wavelength to said first feedback device, and said second feedback device together with said first feedback device and said gain medium defining a resonant cavity substantially parallel to the upper surface of said base, and the second feedback device responsive to the arcuate displacement of said pivot arm 7 to vary the selected wavelength. l

13. A wavelength control system for a tunable laser with a gain medium and a tunable feedback device to provide feedback of a selected output wavelength to the gain medium and the tunable feedback device responsive to drive signals to vary the selected output wavelength of the tunable laser, and the wavelength control system comprising: a lookup table storing values conelating output wavelength and drive signals relative to a starting position of said tunable feedback device; a start indicator coupled to the tunable feedback device to indicate the starting position of said tunable feedback device; and a first logic coupled to said start indicator, the tunable feedback device and said lookup table, and said first logic for generating drive signals to position the tunable feedback device at the starting position as indicated by said start indicator and said first logic responsive to a next selected output wavelength to compare the next selected wavelength to the values in said lookup table and to generate conesponding drive signals to tune the tunable feedback device to the next selected wavelength. 14. The wavelength control system of Claim 13, wherein said start indicator includes at least one of: a position sensor, a cunent sensor, a voltage sensor, a magnetic sensor, and a wavelength sensor. 15. A method for controlling output wavelength in a tunable laser with a gain medium and a tunable feedback device to provide feedback of a selected output wavelength to the gain medium and the tunable feedback device responsive to drive signals to vary the selected output wavelength of the tunable laser, and the method for controlling output wavelength comprising the acts of: 

 storing values conelating output wavelength and drive signals relative to a starting position of the tunable feedback device; positioning the tunable feedback device at the starting position; selecting a next selected output wavelength; comparing the next selected output wavelength to the values stored in said act of storing; calculating the drive signals required to re-position the tunable feedback device at the next selected output wavelength responsive to said act of comparing; and generating the drive signals to tune the tunable feedback device to the next selected wavelength responsive to said act of comparing. 16. A modulation circuit for a tunable laser with a gain medium including a control input and an output, and the output responsive to a variation in a cunent applied to the control input to vary an energy level of an output beam emitted therefrom, and the modulation circuit comprising: a current source having a control input and a source, and a current level at the source determined by a level of an enor signal applied to the control input; a setpoint module having an output, and the setpoint module generating a setpoint signal at the output; an enor integrator having an optical input, a setpoint input, and an output, coupled to respectively the output of the gain medium, the output of said setpoint module and the control input of said cunent source, and said enor integrator supplying at the output the enor signal at a level conesponding to an integration of the enor between the energy level of the output beam and the setpoint signal; a first switch switchably coupling and uncoupling the source of said current source with the control input of the gain medium in respectively a closed state and an open state; 

 a second switch switchably coupling and uncoupling the output of said setpoint module and the setpoint input of said enor integrator in respectively the closed state and the open state; and a control unit coupled to said first switch and said second switch to substantially synchronously switch both said first switch and said second switch between the open state and the closed state to modulate the output beam. 17. The modulation circuit of Claim 16, wherein the control unit substantially synchronously switches said first switch and said second switch to modulate the output beam on at least one of: a selected frequency and a selected duty cycle. 18. A method for modulating a tunable laser with a gain medium responsive to a variation in an applied cunent to vary an energy of an output beam emitted therefrom, and the method for modulating comprising the acts of: supplying a setpoint signal; generating a control signal alternating between an on state and an off state; supplying, during the on state, the applied cunent to the gain medium at a level conesponding to an integration of an error between the energy of the output beam and the setpoint signal; and holding, during the off state, the applied cunent at substantially a prior level of the applied cunent during the on state. 19. The method for modulating of Claim 18, wherein the generating act further comprising the act of: alternating between the on state and the off state on at least one of: a selected frequency and a selected duty cycle.
